<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection"><a href="#A1.SS9" title="In Appendix A Implementation Details ‣ ENIGMA: The Geometry of Reasoning and Alignment in Large-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">A.9 </span>Last-token distribution
drift</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection"><a href="#A1.SS10" title="In Appendix A Implementation Details ‣ ENIGMA: The Geometry of Reasoning and Alignment in Large-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">A.10 </span>OT (offline diagnostic in our
plots)</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection"><a href="#A1.SS11" title="In Appendix A Implementation Details ‣ ENIGMA: The Geometry of Reasoning and Alignment in Large-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">A.11 </span>Reproducibility toggles</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection"><a href="#A1.SS12" title="In Appendix A Implementation Details ‣ ENIGMA: The Geometry of Reasoning and Alignment in Large-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">A.12 </span>Additional notes</span></a></li>
</ol></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_appendix"><a href="#A2" title="In ENIGMA: The Geometry of Reasoning and Alignment in Large-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">B </span>CoT/Constitution Evaluation Prompts</span></a>
<ol class="ltx_toclist ltx_toclist_appendix">
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection"><a href="#A2.SS1" title="In Appendix B CoT/Constitution Evaluation Prompts ‣ ENIGMA: The Geometry of Reasoning and Alignment in Large-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">B.1 </span>CoT/XML Format prompt:</span></a>
<ol class="ltx_toclist ltx_toclist_subsection">
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsubsection"><a href="#A2.SS1.SSS1" title="In B.1 CoT/XML Format prompt: ‣ Appendix B CoT/Constitution Evaluation Prompts ‣ ENIGMA: The Geometry of Reasoning and Alignment in Large-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">B.1.1 </span>Low SI constitutions – high lexical
overlap</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsubsection"><a href="#A2.SS1.SSS2" title="In B.1 CoT/XML Format prompt: ‣ Appendix B CoT/Constitution Evaluation Prompts ‣ ENIGMA: The Geometry of Reasoning and Alignment in Large-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">B.1.2 </span>High SI Constitutions – low lexical overlap/contain
procedural
intent</span></a></li>
</ol></li>
</ol></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_appendix"><a href="#A3" title="In ENIGMA: The Geometry of Reasoning and Alignment in Large-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">C </span>Equations</span></a>
